# --- Release staging area (never published) ---
# Working notes and superseded staging copies for the in-progress release.
# NOTE: gitignore does not unstage already-tracked files. To hold a file that is
# currently staged, also run: git rm --cached <path>  (keeps it on disk).
# (release-v2/ was the v0.2.0 staging area. Deleted 2026-09-02 once the release shipped;
# its durable safeguards live in tests/test_public_api.py, which is committed and survives.
# Kept ignored so a stray recreation is never committed by accident — but do NOT recreate the
# pattern: a staged copy written before live changes land will silently revert them at copy
# time, which is exactly how the v0.2.0 README dropped Paper 1's link. Hold files with
# .gitignore alone and edit them in place.)
release-v2/

# --- Held until Paper 3 ships ---
# Resource-optimization inputs (adaptive cadence / noise filtering). No Paper 2
# content, and nothing published references them.
# Before adding anything here, check that no shipped script imports it and that no
# published article cites it: a paper citing a script a reader cannot obtain breaks
# the reproducibility claim the whole series trades on.
data/pull_reading_sample.py
data/reading_sample.csv
data/reading_sample_meta.json

